  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_5165e898c23c4ff5bb886a3cfce96309",
      "statement": "Every BFF Keycloak Admin REST API call authenticates by minting an admin token from a dedicated service account: getAdminToken() in keycloak.ts POSTs grant_type=client_credentials with keycloakServiceClientId/keycloakServiceClientSecret to the realm's token endpoint and returns the access_token, and any non-OK token response is mapped to an AuthError with code KEYCLOAK_UNAVAILABLE and HTTP status 503 (never 401), so a wrong or missing service-account secret is indistinguishable from Keycloak being down.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L67-L93",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0a8072a82522660a4a2b3aeb2f1d96dbe6e2e806180ddf6b61e0b3435268e6ce:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/unit-tests/email-service.test.ts#L133-L140",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:40b5ff92d30df9a511a3ab5c45ef243fe848f2198d4d0b9349acef52fefa680d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5112cfcad0c24427a4f460e258910662",
      "statement": "The service-account credentials are a separate client from the user-facing login client: env.ts defines keycloakServiceClientId (KEYCLOAK_SERVICE_CLIENT_ID, default mcm-bff-service) and keycloakServiceClientSecret alongside the distinct keycloakClientId (KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID) and keycloakClientSecret used for the authorization-code and refresh grants, so one client's credentials must not be reused for the other's grant type.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L101-L165",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:50f65fe71454fc9911844e814673bf5ce53fc5aa594fbdebc6bc28ee3f34ce7e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/config/env.ts#L19-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:846983ff33f072fadf62419069786c8d36bbfec667fe0981038447673bfaffbf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8ab46d0d1f894d13bbdf5abec4c7f05c",
      "statement": "email-service.ts carries its own duplicated getAdminToken() rather than importing keycloak.ts's, to avoid a circular dependency, and the two copies are not identical: keycloak.ts's copy goes through a keycloakFetch wrapper that adds the request's X-Request-Id header while email-service.ts's copy calls bare fetch, and sendVerificationEmail reads the client id from env.keycloakClientId in one copy and keycloakConfig.clientId in the other — so a change to the grant parameters, error handling or endpoint has to be applied in both places.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/email-service.ts#L11-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d9012a2fbac75e98ada1b572de05267eee882df236f0c1de4a1b7a493459f51:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L13-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ba87727f87aba81a5a10106bea01960f9f4af896e5e87147307f1bb88b54bec:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L375-L394",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6a145f6236cc7249245c0b1b29b5aee872e85b37324926afcffc9957198e1d47:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_68a9552718e54f209c14345c998083ae",
      "statement": "A service account whose realm-management client roles (view-users, manage-clients, manage-users — seeded for service-account-mcm-bff-service in the committed realm) are missing still authenticates, so the 503 token path never triggers, and Keycloak rejects each Admin API call with 403 which the BFF re-maps per caller instead of passing through: deleteUser, countUsersInClientRole and sendVerificationEmail answer 502 KEYCLOAK_UNAVAILABLE, createUser answers 400 INVALID_INPUT, and logoutUserSessions ignores the failure entirely — a 403 is therefore never visible in a BFF response.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/email-service.ts#L43-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab170ad4bafc9eeb489a6c99605e6607e3033f9c8d404cfd65cc4fdbc0e7b0fa:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L189-L255",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:075b9c3a39eaae1d538110e89cb4d1874a5bd6d00080937c8ca782516d1b2cbc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L313-L322",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:723e8fc85b8e58ab88b8b20bbe006e8675cbd3654209a5cc14f3a7c77f8ac16d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/keycloak/ci-realm.json",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:54006ba1df683356ac1a321a914c8bcd78df95ab6b60e79927d728859a5275d6"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_302bd8b93cc04b6fbf265fb9e145a0aa",
      "statement": "deleteUser treats a 404 from the Admin API as success and throws KEYCLOAK_UNAVAILABLE with status 502 for any other non-OK response, because account deletion's identity step is the last and irreversible one and a retry after a partial failure re-issues the delete against an account the first attempt already removed — treating 404 as an error would make the retry fail exactly where it had otherwise worked.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L174-L206",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b310079c8bcc2c424d887a4a95ce3988027edd0c10bb5bda38f812c7b0fc47e0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/unit-tests/keycloak-delete-user.test.ts#L38-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44e99dd4e5948b14445df1f87e14cc6e6ba49614b905e2c1127bf5aa3c339581:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3bc02ca8399343febb996e52da55bda9",
      "statement": "ensureClientRedirectUris(uris, keycloakClientId) is a second Admin API path that mints an admin token, looks up the named client, and PUTs the client representation back with [...existing, ...missing]; feature 083 added the keycloakClientId parameter (defaulting to the login client) so the backup-consent client's own callback can be registered on that client, because on the login client alone Keycloak refuses the consent authorization request. Its entire body is wrapped in a try with a bare catch that swallows every failure, so a service account without manage-clients or a Keycloak outage silently leaves the redirect URI unregistered, unlogged and unreported, and the operator must add the entry by hand.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/init%2Bapi.ts#L23-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:273eb767ad53f12b9920b5aa1493012793e4deba911d3cea01398149001f7284:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L461-L519",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d798638a3b4a496413ba0d634762e0d8cbbd1afb7546d90ebdbccab341977c3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/tests/integration/backup-consent-redirect-uri.integration.test.ts#L46-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6792451554c7f7bddcf94ece5cab6238e1efe33692ffd95184fc52cc26878ed8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9c5874452a744b84b6e84930ef5df7fb",
      "statement": "ensureClientRedirectUris is one-shot per Keycloak client id per process lifetime, tracked in a module-level Set, and the client id is recorded only after a successful run — so a call that failed is retried on the next GET /bff-api/auth/init rather than being permanently skipped.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L463-L475",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1d6fcdaa9d54021c06ef22b5e662a4e73e51f9bd2d37dc8ac661f916382e118f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L514-L519",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:99c37da42ff000d43dc3a47804699201d5363a445cbfd025af58d5013a1c83e0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_10872e548be24976a84cf8aaeb7846d5",
      "statement": "The admin token is minted per call and never cached: each Admin API function in keycloak.ts calls getAdminToken() itself (unlike the OIDC discovery document, which is cached at module level), so one user-facing operation makes several token requests — registration mints for createUser, assignMcUserRole and sendVerificationEmail, and the resend-verification route mints once for getUserIdByEmail and again for sendVerificationEmail — and a rotated or mistyped service-account secret takes every Admin API call down at once rather than degrading it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/register%2Bapi.ts#L80-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2ad40f066e0bbbadd45bb811fc44956700e8f6985932f7a432f09392701f6408:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/resend-verification%2Bapi.ts#L36-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:715014ef0049c64606bb737d70c23d2a0725ff83ae0652b11997738b2f4cefba:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L42-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:92e097d480d417e469f1d5651f9a7c23d6eb8d72cb5a2d81adfc4d4fe625640f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6986a639259143c9b8a05600dc0307e6",
      "statement": "Two Admin API callers hide failures rather than reporting them: getUserIdByEmail returns null for any non-OK Admin response (indistinguishable from 'no such user'), and assignMcUserRole never inspects the HTTP response of its role-mapping POST. Combined with /bff-api/auth/resend-verification deliberately answering success for an unknown email (so the endpoint is not a user-enumeration oracle), a service account that lost view-users or manage-users produces a success response while the underlying operation did nothing — a registration can report success with the mc-user role unassigned, and the user is then refused by the role gate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/resend-verification%2Bapi.ts#L40-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6024b22582d59719eb2d4990eb72691d0ebfb2b0f02dffcf986f193b867222cf:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L337-L369",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:57e788f6af9387fb7f17ee9dbcca120e1eeab17bd6c3e4b16b3990e41bbbf0a6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L402-L419",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a87e32810ef8a985dc6c7b79ff9c8ceb46d2ef6c1a689c2b5064247ace91eaa3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b08e94d4af334ae7ae3449fcee84b453",
      "statement": "The swallowed Admin API failures are not uniform and the differences are deliberate: deleteUser counts 404 as success for retry safety; logoutUserSessions and revokeToken ignore failures because the BFF session and token are already gone and the token expires naturally; and backup-offline-token.ts deliberately does not reuse revokeToken, reporting whether the revocation succeeded instead, because an offline refresh token never expires and so has no such backstop.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/backup-offline-token.ts#L291-L315",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5f23cc70a0ec1f8178b76478bb7c7f5e7e0a35d9e0e7663b720443b32c7fb469:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L245-L281",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8588153a84f1824dd6efbac1c12d98f41f118f309035f68bf037225508fc6e60:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e5e54bf5a3d24f09acb058f7296474df",
      "statement": "The account-deletion pipeline uses both credential sets in one ordered run: account-deletion.ts calls deleteUser and logoutUserSessions (service-account Admin API) alongside revokeToken (the app client's revoke endpoint), with deleteIdentity last because it is the only irreversible step — so a 503 from the Admin API steps says nothing about the token-revocation step, and deleteUser's 404-as-success rule is what makes a retry of that pipeline completable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/account-deletion.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:a924ef36ed39ea119bbfd638eb4b005c0c4d483b7a065238bd1261f583db6c46"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L189-L206",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b9899652d9066df727bd28766b760ddc2f815a610907d6e7eba2f640c8233d20:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_535aacced10c4a4d8d8dc875eb052a01",
      "statement": "countUsersInClientRole throws KEYCLOAK_UNAVAILABLE with status 502 when the client lookup or the role-members listing fails, rather than returning 0, because a failed count must not read as 'no administrators exist' and let the last administrator delete themselves.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/keycloak.ts#L208-L243",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:790c92eca6692c09f72267619e029bc9e0843ec45d9ea4e5b3d70672ab08843c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_541ef94efb774cd98f3731f295167d3e",
      "statement": "A Keycloak realm partial-export does not carry service-account role mappings, so the committed realm files reconstruct them explicitly as service-account-<clientId> users with realmRoles and clientRoles; without that reconstruction a partial import yields a service account that mints tokens and authorizes nothing, and every Admin API call it makes comes back 403.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/keycloak/ci-realm.json",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:54006ba1df683356ac1a321a914c8bcd78df95ab6b60e79927d728859a5275d6"
        },
